From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GD Sistemas <dev@gdsistemas.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] libcxx: avoid socket sendfile for Orbis copy_file

OpenOrbis exposes the BSD/FreeBSD sendfile API, whose destination is a
socket and whose signature is incompatible with libc++'s Linux-style
file-to-file copy implementation.

Use libc++'s fstream fallback for std::filesystem::copy_file on Orbis.
---
 libcxx/src/filesystem/operations.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libcxx/src/filesystem/operations.cpp b/libcxx/src/filesystem/operations.cpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/libcxx/src/filesystem/operations.cpp
+++ b/libcxx/src/filesystem/operations.cpp
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #include <fcntl.h> /* values for fchmodat */
 #include <time.h>
 
-#if __has_include(<sys/sendfile.h>)
+#if !defined(__ORBIS__) && __has_include(<sys/sendfile.h>)
 #  include <sys/sendfile.h>
 #  define _LIBCPP_FILESYSTEM_USE_SENDFILE
 #elif defined(__APPLE__) || __has_include(<copyfile.h>)
-- 
2.43.0
